1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:2aed19f847ef406ae9e4845e190582bf294180414b2becded16a2ff8a080d709","file":"preprints/Kadisons-similarity-theorem-through-uniform-derivation-estimates-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":109,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"fefdc3607780987fc20f89c1f3b5e0cd024eafadd9fe5c0dcb4fcf98ea02e128","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Kadisons-similarity-theorem-through-uniform-derivation-estimates-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2aed19f847ef406ae9e4845e190582bf294180414b2becded16a2ff8a080d709","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Kadisons-similarity-theorem-through-uniform-derivation-estimates-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L109"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:universal}\nThere is an absolute constant \\(C<\\infty\\) such that, for every complex\nHilbert space \\(K\\), every unital von Neumann algebra\n\\(P\\subset\\mathcal B(K)\\), every \\(Y\\in\\mathcal B(K)\\), every integer\n\\(h\\ge1\\), and every \\(X\\in M_h(P)\\),\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:universal}\n  \\|[Y^{(h)},X]\\|\\le C\\,g_P(Y)\\,\\|X\\|.\n\\end{equation}\nHere \\(M_h(P)\\) acts naturally on \\(K^h\\), and \\([T,U]=TU-UT\\)."}
